From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 23:35:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Gate per-resolve work on damage

Several passes in resolve re-derived their output from scratch every
frame, each one a pure function of state that mostly had not changed.

Tree walks. On a 271k-node page with ten damaged nodes,
resolve_layout_children made 42.6k visits and opened its construct
gate zero times, and compute_rehomed_reach ran two full-slab scans for
hosts that usually do not exist. resolve_layout_children now returns
early on a clean subtree, keyed on the damaged-descendants flag; like
propagate_damage_flags it still enters anonymous boxes and shadow
hosts, which damage marking does not reach, and a node with no cached
children re-collects as before. The end-of-resolve damage clear enters
shadow trees for the same reason. compute_rehomed_reach tracks its
hosts at the single push site and remembers the chains it wrote, so it
clears and rescans only those. Construct 2.9ms -> 0.13ms, rehomed reach
2.2ms -> 41ns.

Counters. counters_seen is a sticky positive (one list item anywhere
turns it on for good, and most navigation menus trip it) after which
resolve_counters rebuilt the whole tree every resolve. Output is a
function of tree shape and the counter-affecting styles alone, so gate
on CONSTRUCT damage: structural mutations stamp ALL_DAMAGE, and display
/ list-style / content / counter-* diffs all rebuild the box tree (the
counter-* diff is added here), so every input that can move a counter
is covered while plain RELAYOUT damage cannot. On a 65k-node document
that took counters from 8.3ms to 0.95ms. Answering the gate still meant
a slab scan to prove a negative on paint-only frames, so
accumulate_damage_summary now records whether any damage was CONSTRUCT
damage and moves ahead of resolve_counters, and the gate reads the
flag: 2.1ms -> 41ns.

Ordering is what makes that last fusion safe. Exactly one thing raises
damage between the summary and where the gate used to run:
damage_moved_counters, which stamps CONSTRUCT_BOX on the counters it saw
move. That set is explicit rather than discovered by scanning, so it is
handed to note_late_layout_damage, which folds it into the summary.
Dropping it fails renumber_reaches_an_undamaged_subtree: inserting into
one list renumbers a sibling list that carries no damage of its own,
and the construct walk would never reach it.

Rounding. round_layout is a pure function of the unrounded layouts, so
set_unrounded_layout notes whether any box actually moved, and resolve
skips the rounding walk when none did. restore_clobbered_inline_breaks
skips on the same signal plus a count of inline roots it has settled;
debug builds run it anyway and assert it finds nothing.

Skipping round_layout means a post-layout shift can no longer assume
taffy just wiped the location: a sticky shift re-applied with no ledger
accumulated across skipped passes. Node::pin_offset records what is
baked into a location and is zeroed by set_final_layout, the single
place a location is written wholesale, and set_pin_offset states the
shift absolutely and reconciles the delta. note_boxes_moved bumps the
geometry generation for such a move, which is what memoised paint
positions key on.
